{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show cf495f1b; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc | sed -n '45,220p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md | sed -n '86,108p'\"","aggregated_output":"commit cf495f1b6b360b8c06dabf146f86f0ff96dced04\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Oct 5 01:22:33 2026 +0700\n\n    fix(yin.repl): refuse a saved flag with no value, a state file that cannot be read, and a non-keyword setting\n    \n    Review findings P2 missing value resolving to the saved one, P2 raw I/O error bypassing the refusal, P4 name on a non-keyword key; and the shared-directory doc now names every unprotected case.\n\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc\nindex 0f1acfee..524a4f45 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc\n@@ -46,11 +46,22 @@\n   #{\"--dht-manifest\" \"--dht-keygen\"})\n \n \n+(defn- value-of\n+  \"The value after `flag`, or a refusal: a missing value (or another flag\n+   in its place) must never fall back to the saved one.\"\n+  [flag more]\n+  (let [value (first more)]\n+    (if (and (some? value) (not (str/starts-with? value \"--\")))\n+      value\n+      (throw (ex-info (str flag \" needs a value\") {:flag flag})))))\n+\n+\n (defn split-args\n   \"Split `args` into `{:flags {flag value} :rest [arg ...]}`: the flags a\n    state file keeps (a switch is `true`, a repeated flag a vector) and\n-   everything else, in order, for the arguments parser.  A valued flag with\n-   no value stays in `:rest` so the parser refuses it as it always has.\"\n+   everything else, in order, for the arguments parser.  A saved flag or a\n+   one-shot flag with no value is refused here, before it can be resolved\n+   against the saved value.\"\n   [args]\n   (loop [args (seq args) flags {} rest []]\n     (if-let [arg (first args)]\n@@ -59,16 +70,16 @@\n         (cond\n           (= :switch kind) (recur more (assoc flags arg true) rest)\n \n-          (and (#{:value :many} kind) (seq more))\n-          (let [value (first more)]\n+          (#{:value :many} kind)\n+          (let [value (value-of arg more)]\n             (recur (next more)\n                    (if (= :many kind)\n                      (update flags arg (fnil conj []) value)\n                      (assoc flags arg value))\n                    rest))\n \n-          (and (one-shot-flags arg) (seq more))\n-          (recur (next more) flags (conj rest arg (first more)))\n+          (one-shot-flags arg)\n+          (recur (next more) flags (conj rest arg (value-of arg more)))\n \n           :else (recur more flags (conj rest arg))))\n       {:flags flags :rest rest})))\n@@ -150,8 +161,8 @@\n \n       :else\n       (reduce (fn [flags [k v]]\n-                (let [flag (str \"--\" (name k))\n-                      kind (kinds flag)]\n+                (let [kind (when (keyword? k) (kinds (str \"--\" (name k))))\n+                      flag (when kind (str \"--\" (name k)))]\n                   (cond\n                     (nil? kind)\n                     (throw (refuse path (str \"unknown setting \" (pr-str k))))\n@@ -183,7 +194,15 @@\n    state file.  A file that cannot be understood is refused, never\n    skipped.\"\n   [dir]\n-  (when-some [text (fs/read-file-text dir file-name)]\n+  (when-some [text (try (fs/read-file-text dir file-name)\n+                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n+                                  :clj Throwable\n+                                  :cljs :default)\n+                               e\n+                          (throw (refuse (path dir)\n+                                         (str \"it cannot be read (\"\n+                                              (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n+                                              \")\")))))]\n     (text->config (path dir) text)))\n \n \ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md b/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\nindex 1e9e18f9..acc77f21 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\n@@ -92,9 +92,13 @@ file is plain EDN and may be edited by hand:\n   is a warning, and the node still starts.\n - **Hosts:** ClojureDart has no home directory, so a bare `yin-repl` there\n   saves nothing unless `--dir` names the node directory.\n-- **One node per directory:** a `file:` or `dht:` store's lock already keeps\n-  one process per directory. A node on the in-memory store has no lock, so\n-  two such processes with the same name would overwrite each other's file.\n+- **One node per name:** the state file is only as protected as its\n+  directory. `dht init|serve|join` put the store in the node directory, so the\n+  store's lock also keeps one process per state file. A node whose store lives\n+  elsewhere (`--index-store file:/tmp/a`, or the in-memory default) is not\n+  covered: two such processes with the same `--name` or `--dir` overwrite each\n+  other's file, last writer wins, and no process notices. Give each its own\n+  `--name`.\n \n ## Protocol and Architecture\n \ndiff --git a/test/yin/repl/state_test.cljc b/test/yin/repl/state_test.cljc\nindex 475dbc74..4ebc2889 100644\n--- a/test/yin/repl/state_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yin/repl/state_test.cljc\n@@ -23,16 +23,25 @@\n   (let [{:keys [flags rest]}\n         (state/split-args [\"--port\" \"8080\" \"--headless\" \"--dht-peer\" \"a:1\"\n                            \"--dht-peer\" \"b:2\" \"--dht-manifest\" \":segment/x\"\n-                           \"--telemetry\" \"--vm\"])]\n+                           \"--telemetry\"])]\n     (is (= {\"--port\" \"8080\" \"--headless\" true \"--dht-peer\" [\"a:1\" \"b:2\"]}\n            flags))\n     (testing \"one-shot flags and unknown arguments pass through, in order\"\n-      (is (= [\"--dht-manifest\" \":segment/x\" \"--telemetry\" \"--vm\"] rest)))\n+      (is (= [\"--dht-manifest\" \":segment/x\" \"--telemetry\"] rest)))\n     (is (= [\"--port\" \"8080\" \"--headless\" \"--dht-peer\" \"a:1\" \"--dht-peer\" \"b:2\"]\n            (state/flags->args flags))\n         \"a fixed order, a repeated flag once per value\")))\n \n \n+(deftest a-flag-with-no-value-is-refused-not-resolved-to-the-saved-one\n+  (doseq [args [[\"--port\"] [\"--port\" \"--headless\"] [\"--vm\"] [\"--dht-peer\"]\n+                [\"--dht-peer\" \"a:1\" \"--dht-peer\"] [\"--dht-manifest\"]\n+                [\"--dht-keygen\" \"--help\"]]]\n+    (let [e (refusal-of #(state/split-args args))]\n+      (is (some? (ex-data e)) (pr-str args))\n+      (is (str/includes? (ex-message e) \"needs a value\") (pr-str args)))))\n+\n+\n (deftest the-command-line-replaces-saved-values-whole\n   (let [saved {\"--dht-peer\" [\"a:1\"] \"--dht-publish\" true \"--port\" \"1\"}]\n     (is (= {\"--dht-peer\" [\"b:2\" \"c:3\"] \"--dht-publish\" true \"--port\" \"1\"}\n@@ -66,6 +75,8 @@\n                       [\"{:version 2 :config {}}\" \"version-1\"]\n                       [\"{:version 1}\" \":config\"]\n                       [\"{:version 1 :config {:nonsense \\\"x\\\"}}\" \"unknown setting\"]\n+                      [\"{:version 1 :config {42 \\\"x\\\"}}\" \"unknown setting\"]\n+                      [\"{:version 1 :config {\\\"--port\\\" \\\"1\\\"}}\" \"unknown setting\"]\n                       [\"{:version 1 :config {:port 8080}}\" \"must be a string\"]\n                       [\"{:version 1 :config {:dht-peer \\\"a:1\\\"}}\"\n                        \"vector of strings\"]\n@@ -79,6 +90,34 @@\n         (is (str/includes? (ex-message e) \"--reset\") text)))))\n \n \n+;; Dart's File.existsSync is false for a directory, so the path reads as\n+;; absent there: this scenario is a JVM and Node one.\n+(deftest a-state-path-that-cannot-be-read-is-refused-naming-the-file\n+  #?(:cljd nil\n+     :default\n+     (let [dir (temp-dir)]\n+       ;; a directory where the file should be: existing, but not readable text\n+       (state/save! (str dir \"/\" state/file-name) {})\n+       (let [e (refusal-of #(state/load-flags dir))]\n+         (is (some? (ex-data e)) \"a designed refusal, not a raw I/O exception\")\n+         (is (str/includes? (ex-message e) \"cannot be read\"))\n+         (is (str/includes? (ex-message e) \"--reset\")))\n+       (let [started (repl/startup [\"--dir\" dir] {:persist? true})]\n+         (is (str/includes? (:refusal started) \"cannot be read\"))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest a-missing-value-never-starts-with-the-saved-one\n+  (let [dir (temp-dir)]\n+    (state/save! dir {\"--port\" \"8080\"})\n+    (doseq [args [[\"--port\"] [\"--port\" \"9000\" \"--port\"]]]\n+      (let [started (repl/startup (into [\"--dir\" dir] args) {:persist? true})]\n+        (is (str/includes? (:refusal started) \"--port needs a value\")\n+            (pr-str args))\n+        (is (nil? (:state started)))))\n+    (is (= {\"--port\" \"8080\"} (state/load-flags dir))\n+        \"a refused start saves nothing\")))\n+\n+\n (defn- vm-of\n   [started]\n   (get-in started [:state :repl :vm-type]))\n    45\t  \"Flags that take a value but are never saved.\"\n    46\t  #{\"--dht-manifest\" \"--dht-keygen\"})\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- value-of\n    50\t  \"The value after `flag`, or a refusal: a missing value (or another flag\n    51\t   in its place) must never fall back to the saved one.\"\n    52\t  [flag more]\n    53\t  (let [value (first more)]\n    54\t    (if (and (some? value) (not (str/starts-with? value \"--\")))\n    55\t      value\n    56\t      (throw (ex-info (str flag \" needs a value\") {:flag flag})))))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defn split-args\n    60\t  \"Split `args` into `{:flags {flag value} :rest [arg ...]}`: the flags a\n    61\t   state file keeps (a switch is `true`, a repeated flag a vector) and\n    62\t   everything else, in order, for the arguments parser.  A saved flag or a\n    63\t   one-shot flag with no value is refused here, before it can be resolved\n    64\t   against the saved value.\"\n    65\t  [args]\n    66\t  (loop [args (seq args) flags {} rest []]\n    67\t    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n    68\t      (let [kind (kinds arg)\n    69\t            more (next args)]\n    70\t        (cond\n    71\t          (= :switch kind) (recur more (assoc flags arg true) rest)\n    72\t\n    73\t          (#{:value :many} kind)\n    74\t          (let [value (value-of arg more)]\n    75\t            (recur (next more)\n    76\t                   (if (= :many kind)\n    77\t                     (update flags arg (fnil conj []) value)\n    78\t                     (assoc flags arg value))\n    79\t                   rest))\n    80\t\n    81\t          (one-shot-flags arg)\n    82\t          (recur (next more) flags (conj rest arg (value-of arg more)))\n    83\t\n    84\t          :else (recur more flags (conj rest arg))))\n    85\t      {:flags flags :rest rest})))\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn flags->args\n    89\t  \"The argument vector that says `flags`, in a fixed order.\"\n    90\t  [flags]\n    91\t  (into []\n    92\t        (mapcat (fn [[flag kind]]\n    93\t                  (when-some [v (get flags flag)]\n    94\t                    (case kind\n    95\t                      :switch (when (true? v) [flag])\n    96\t                      :value [flag v]\n    97\t                      :many (mapcat (fn [x] [flag x]) v)))))\n    98\t        saved-flags))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn resolve-flags\n   102\t  \"The flags this run starts with: `saved` overridden by `explicit`, minus\n   103\t   the `unset` flags a subcommand clears (`dht serve` is never publishing,\n   104\t   whatever was saved).\"\n   105\t  [saved explicit unset]\n   106\t  (apply dissoc (merge saved explicit) unset))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn changed\n   110\t  \"The flags, sorted, whose value in `resolved` differs from `saved`.\"\n   111\t  [saved resolved]\n   112\t  (->> (concat (keys saved) (keys resolved))\n   113\t       distinct\n   114\t       (remove #(= (get saved %) (get resolved %)))\n   115\t       sort\n   116\t       vec))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn describe\n   120\t  \"`flags` as one line of `--flag value` text.\"\n   121\t  [flags]\n   122\t  (str/join \", \"\n   123\t            (for [[flag _] saved-flags\n   124\t                  :let [v (get flags flag)]\n   125\t                  :when (some? v)]\n   126\t              (cond\n   127\t                (true? v) flag\n   128\t                (vector? v) (str/join \", \" (map #(str flag \" \" %) v))\n   129\t                :else (str flag \" \" v)))))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(defn- config-key\n   133\t  [flag]\n   134\t  (keyword (subs flag 2)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn- refuse\n   138\t  [path why]\n   139\t  (ex-info (str \"state file \" path \": \" why \"; --reset replaces it\")\n   140\t           {:path path}))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn- text->config\n   144\t  \"The flags a state file's text holds, or a refusal naming `path`.\"\n   145\t  [path text]\n   146\t  (let [data (try #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n   147\t                     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n   148\t                     :cljs (reader/read-string text))\n   149\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   150\t                            :clj Throwable\n   151\t                            :cljs :default)\n   152\t                         _\n   153\t                    (throw (refuse path \"it is not readable EDN\"))))\n   154\t        config (when (map? data) (:config data))]\n   155\t    (cond\n   156\t      (not (and (map? data) (= version (:version data))))\n   157\t      (throw (refuse path (str \"it is not a version-\" version \" state file\")))\n   158\t\n   159\t      (not (map? config))\n   160\t      (throw (refuse path \"it has no :config map\"))\n   161\t\n   162\t      :else\n   163\t      (reduce (fn [flags [k v]]\n   164\t                (let [kind (when (keyword? k) (kinds (str \"--\" (name k))))\n   165\t                      flag (when kind (str \"--\" (name k)))]\n   166\t                  (cond\n   167\t                    (nil? kind)\n   168\t                    (throw (refuse path (str \"unknown setting \" (pr-str k))))\n   169\t\n   170\t                    (and (= :switch kind) (not (true? v)))\n   171\t                    (throw (refuse path (str (pr-str k) \" must be true\")))\n   172\t\n   173\t                    (and (= :value kind) (not (string? v)))\n   174\t                    (throw (refuse path (str (pr-str k) \" must be a string\")))\n   175\t\n   176\t                    (and (= :many kind)\n   177\t                         (not (and (vector? v) (every? string? v))))\n   178\t                    (throw (refuse path (str (pr-str k) \" must be a vector of\"\n   179\t                                             \" strings\")))\n   180\t\n   181\t                    :else (assoc flags flag v))))\n   182\t              {}\n   183\t              config))))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn path\n   187\t  \"The state file's path in the node directory `dir`.\"\n   188\t  [dir]\n   189\t  (str dir \"/\" file-name))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn load-flags\n   193\t  \"The saved flags in the node directory `dir`, or nil when there is no\n   194\t   state file.  A file that cannot be understood is refused, never\n   195\t   skipped.\"\n   196\t  [dir]\n   197\t  (when-some [text (try (fs/read-file-text dir file-name)\n   198\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   199\t                                  :clj Throwable\n   200\t                                  :cljs :default)\n   201\t                               e\n   202\t                          (throw (refuse (path dir)\n   203\t                                         (str \"it cannot be read (\"\n   204\t                                              (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n   205\t                                              \")\")))))]\n   206\t    (text->config (path dir) text)))\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\t(defn- mkdirs!\n   210\t  [dir]\n   211\t  #?(:cljd (.createSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n   212\t     :clj (.mkdirs (java.io.File. ^String dir))\n   213\t     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\t(defn- render\n   217\t  \"The state file's text, one setting to a line, with no space before a\n   218\t   closing bracket (ClojureDart's EDN reader refuses one).\"\n   219\t  [flags]\n   220\t  (let [entries (for [[flag _] saved-flags\n    86\t- **`--reset`** forgets the saved state and starts from the command line\n    87\t  alone; the result is saved. **`--no-state`** neither reads nor writes it,\n    88\t  for a one-off run.\n    89\t- **Refusals:** a state file that cannot be read, or saved flags that clash\n    90\t  with the command line (saved `--dht-*` flags with `--index-store mem`), refuse\n    91\t  startup, naming the file and `--reset`. A state file that cannot be written\n    92\t  is a warning, and the node still starts.\n    93\t- **Hosts:** ClojureDart has no home directory, so a bare `yin-repl` there\n    94\t  saves nothing unless `--dir` names the node directory.\n    95\t- **One node per name:** the state file is only as protected as its\n    96\t  directory. `dht init|serve|join` put the store in the node directory, so the\n    97\t  store's lock also keeps one process per state file. A node whose store lives\n    98\t  elsewhere (`--index-store file:/tmp/a`, or the in-memory default) is not\n    99\t  covered: two such processes with the same `--name` or `--dir` overwrite each\n   100\t  other's file, last writer wins, and no process notices. Give each its own\n   101\t  `--name`.\n   102\t\n   103\t## Protocol and Architecture\n   104\t\n   105\t**`connect` returns immediately and reports its outcome when known.**\n   106\t`connect` composes the client boundary, attaches, and answers at once with\n   107\t`Attaching to …`; the driver prints `Connected to …` when the boundary\n   108\treports `/established`, and reports `/not-found` (an authoritative disclaimer,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
